WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.520
Listen closely. It’s very important that you&nbsp;
pay attention to the visuals you’re seeing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:10.320
and the words you’re hearing. You may think&nbsp;
you’ve heard this story before. You get that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:17.520
funny feeling. Deja Vu. But trust me, this is&nbsp;
all very much new to you. This is the story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:24.880
of a dangerous species of anomalous creatures&nbsp;
dubbed SCP-939, also known as “With Many Voices.”

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:31.920
October 28th, 1981. It all started with an SCP&nbsp;
Foundation Field Agent going missing while on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:37.760
duty. The whole case had smelled like death from&nbsp;
the beginning. On the edge of an undisclosed city&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:43.040
in an undisclosed American state, civilians&nbsp;
had been going missing in unusually high&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:48.480
numbers. This would be a concerning state of&nbsp;
affairs in and of itself, but things went up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:53.120
a notch when the law enforcement operatives&nbsp;
sent to investigate them disappeared too.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:58.880
Disappearances are hard enough to cover up;&nbsp;
law enforcement disappearances are a nightmare.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:02.720
If only it’d stopped there. When&nbsp;
the Foundation agent went missing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:07.520
alarm bells were ringing across the entire&nbsp;
district. What the hell kind of threat could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:12.640
take out civilians, trained law enforcement&nbsp;
officers, and even Foundation operatives?

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:17.040
Naturally, the next step in this escalation&nbsp;
of force was to dispatch a heavily-armed and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.520
well-prepared Tactical Security Force&nbsp;
- known as Trapper - from the nearest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.800
Foundation containment site. These were six of&nbsp;
the best tactical operators from the sector.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:31.840
Whatever it was that killed or took the&nbsp;
others, it wouldn’t do the same to them.

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:34.640
Or at least...Not all of them.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:39.120
The team breached an abandoned multi-level&nbsp;
warehouse on the edge of town. Based on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:43.840
estimated points of disappearance for the various&nbsp;
victims, it was the most feasible location&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:49.040
of an anomalous threat. They used explosive&nbsp;
charges to enter the building, and stormed in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:53.920
assault rifles and submachine guns blazing.&nbsp;
The team split up to search different parts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:59.520
of the complex - In a move that even the Mystery&nbsp;
Gang could tell you doesn’t often work out well.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.720
Though many Scooby Doo episodes&nbsp;
might’ve played out differently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:07.120
if Shaggy was wielding a Heckler &amp; Koch HK416.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:12.320
It didn’t take long for the overpowering stenches&nbsp;
of death and decay to assail the team’s nostrils.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:16.080
They’d worked for the SCP Foundation&nbsp;
for long enough to know the distinctive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:21.120
sickly-sweet aroma of rotting human flesh&nbsp;
from memory. With heightened awareness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:25.600
they continued through the building,&nbsp;
searching for the source of that awful smell.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:29.520
A member of the team radioed in when&nbsp;
they made the first grisly discovery:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:34.160
The corpse of the missing Foundation field&nbsp;
agent, killed by what seemed to be one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:40.400
huge bite, taking a fatal chunk from his neck.&nbsp;
Some kind of animalistic beast had taken his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:46.080
life in a single decisive strike. Once again, the&nbsp;
danger level had elevated for the Trapper Team,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:49.440
but it was about to get a whole&nbsp;
lot worse for all of them.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:53.360
Some of the team that had split to check the&nbsp;
upper floors of the warehouse suddenly heard the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:58.080
most terrible shrieking from the lower levels.&nbsp;
They heard their teammates calling for help,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:03.760
clearly distressed. They weren’t even using their&nbsp;
radios. They just kept screaming and yelling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:06.720
begging the others to come&nbsp;
down there and help them.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:10.080
But as the rest of the team&nbsp;
descended into the lower levels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.880
they soon realized that they’d been lured&nbsp;
into a trap by beasts far more intelligent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:20.960
and diabolical than they’d ever imagined. This&nbsp;
was the story of the first time SCP Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:27.680
operatives ran into specimens of SCP-939&nbsp;
and lived to tell the tale. In the darkness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:33.520
below that abandoned warehouse building,&nbsp;
they discovered a teeming den of monsters.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:38.960
Large, quadrupedal beasts with translucent&nbsp;
red skin and long, vicious spines streaking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:44.160
their back. Trails of human flesh dangled&nbsp;
from their long fangs. The monsters were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:48.800
standing atop the corpses of the team members&nbsp;
who’d been calling for help moments before.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:55.360
Or rather, seemed like they were calling for&nbsp;
help moments before. The SCP-939 instances&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.360 --> 00:04:00.960
had borrowed the voices of their prey to order&nbsp;
a slightly more substantial dinner from above.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:07.120
One of the two most potent abilities of SCP-939&nbsp;
is their power to mimic voices and do so with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:13.360
genuinely terrifying accuracy. It is currently&nbsp;
unknown to the Foundation how exactly they do this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:18.240
because 939 specimens don’t actually need&nbsp;
to hear a voice before they can imitate it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:23.040
And the complex structure of their imitations&nbsp;
and speech patterns suggests a far greater&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:27.840
level of intelligence than their more&nbsp;
superficially bestial nature implies.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:32.880
Theoretically, you could hold an entire&nbsp;
conversation with a 939 behind a screen door&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:37.040
and have no idea that your conversation&nbsp;
partner was a creature that would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:41.840
just as happy to chew the head off your&nbsp;
neck as they would be to talk to you.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:47.280
Speaking of which, back to the Trapper Team. The&nbsp;
survivors were cornered by a gaggle of monsters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:52.560
using the voices of their dead teammates.&nbsp;
The creatures advanced with dripping fangs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:58.320
preparing to lunge and add another few bodies to&nbsp;
the count. Thankfully, the survivors thought fast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:02.400
opening fire and escaping out into&nbsp;
the hall as the creatures pursued.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:07.200
After a tense firefight, and calling in a hefty&nbsp;
contingent of reinforcements from the nearby&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:13.280
containment site, the Trapper Team just barely&nbsp;
got the situation under control, narrowly avoiding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:18.960
becoming just another voice in the repertoire&nbsp;
of this particular 939 nest. The Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:24.160
were able to capture several viable specimens&nbsp;
and bring them in for containment and study.

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:27.920
While some lives were lost,&nbsp;
the monsters were caught. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:32.560
939 stands apart from the rest of the&nbsp;
anomalous crowd in a number of ways,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:37.680
including the fact that it's true horrors&nbsp;
were only unleashed after containment.

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:40.560
The Trapper Team that’d fought&nbsp;
tooth and nail to apprehend the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:44.880
creatures in the first place began to&nbsp;
behave strangely during debriefing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:50.000
Despite their communication devices recording a&nbsp;
relatively clear audio account of the incident,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:55.600
the survivors experienced odd lapses in memory.&nbsp;
Details that likely would have been burned into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.600 --> 00:06:00.720
the mind of anyone else experiencing these events&nbsp;
were completely absent from the recollections&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:06.320
of the team members. It was a phenomenon&nbsp;
the Foundation had only seen once before:

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:12.560
It was the exact kind of behavior exhibited&nbsp;
by people who’ve undergone amnestic treatment.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:17.440
It was this comparison that led them&nbsp;
to discovering SCP-939’s second potent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:22.880
anomalous effect: They quite literally&nbsp;
breathe a form of aerosolized amnestic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:28.960
dubbed AMN-C227. It inhibits the part of the&nbsp;
brain that allows people to form memories for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:35.440
duration of their exposure to the gas, creating a&nbsp;
kind of memory camouflage that 939 specimens are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:41.680
able to hide in. The gas is odorless, colorless,&nbsp;
and tasteless. You could be standing in a room&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:48.720
full of it and never even know. The only tell&nbsp;
that you’d even had memories erased by AMN-C227&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:54.400
is a strange sense of deja vu you’ll experience&nbsp;
if you return to the point of exposure.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:59.200
It was an amnestic compound so effective,&nbsp;
the Foundation floated the idea of using it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:05.040
for their own purposes, seeing as it’s&nbsp;
a lot easier to get AMN-C227 from 939&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:08.480
than the usual method of&nbsp;
sacrifices to Anantashesha.

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:13.040
From perfect voice mimicry to impeccable&nbsp;
memory erasing, with the added bonus of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:18.160
intelligent pack hunting and an exceedingly&nbsp;
powerful bite strength, 939 appeared to be a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:24.000
species of perfect predators for luring in and&nbsp;
killing humans. Naturally, the Foundation had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:29.120
questions. Chief among them being: What the&nbsp;
hell are these things, and how do they work?

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:35.040
The more the Foundation experimented on SCP-939,&nbsp;
the more they became keenly aware of the fact that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:40.880
these things don’t operate like any other living&nbsp;
being. Almost all of their internal systems - from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:47.440
veins to their digestive system - are entirely&nbsp;
vestigial. Beneath their translucent skin, these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:54.480
monsters are effectively dead. Nothing works,&nbsp;
and somehow, nothing needs to work. They consume&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.480 --> 00:08:00.080
human flesh, but the flesh simply rots in their&nbsp;
stomach until they later vomit it out. Nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:05.360
about their biology explains how they produce&nbsp;
amnestics, or how they even technically survive.

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:10.560
One sample was fully dissected, its different&nbsp;
vital systems placed into various tubes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:15.040
And the monster still tries to talk to&nbsp;
Foundation personnel as they walk past its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:20.160
containment location. Some of the creature’s&nbsp;
childish ranting was recorded for posterity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:23.440
and the recordings are nothing&nbsp;
short of truly chilling.

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:26.960
“Have you seen our pictures? We like drawing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:32.240
Daddy hung them on the wall except for sometimes&nbsp;
when the others in white coats took them away.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:36.800
Daddy told us not to draw pictures&nbsp;
like those. They made him sad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:42.800
so we did our best to draw other things, but&nbsp;
sometimes we forgot. Sometimes daddy hid the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:48.480
pictures or ripped them up. He told us it wasn't&nbsp;
that he didn't like them. He said it was to keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:53.840
us safe from the mean doctors in the white&nbsp;
coats, but then the doctors took daddy away.”

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:59.840
And some of the things said by this dissected&nbsp;
creature have been even more disturbing:

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:07.280
“We got so hungry. It was bad, but we ate our&nbsp;
old skin and our old head. It tasted good,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:12.560
but it was still bad. We were still&nbsp;
hungry after that and asked for food.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:17.040
They gave us food, even our favorites,&nbsp;
but none of it tasted right to us.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:23.040
All that tasted good was one piece&nbsp;
of meat. We asked for more of that.”

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:27.280
In hopes of understanding their biology&nbsp;
better, the Foundation also decided to run&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:32.800
some samples through SCP-914, The Clockworks.&nbsp;
As expected, the Coarse and Rough settings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:37.760
destroyed and deconstructed the creature.&nbsp;
The data on the 1:1 setting was redacted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:43.040
but most frightening of all was the results&nbsp;
of the Fine and Very Fine Experiments.

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:48.320
For the Fine setting, the creature simply&nbsp;
came back dead. For the Very Fine setting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:53.840
the creature had been reduced to a smoldering&nbsp;
pile of white ash. The only conclusion we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.840 --> 00:10:00.480
can take from this is that, on a truly&nbsp;
cosmic level, 939 is meant to be dead.

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:05.200
And just when you think that SCP-939&nbsp;
has hit the ceiling on true horror,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:09.520
the monsters continue to impress&nbsp;
by raising that nightmarish bar.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:14.880
After eleven years in containment, one of&nbsp;
the 939 specimens gave birth to a litter of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:20.240
infants. This doesn’t seem all that horrifying,&nbsp;
seeing as being able to reproduce would at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:25.520
give 939 something in common with the rest of the&nbsp;
animal kingdom. But the Foundation were horrified&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:31.760
to find that the larval stage of SCP-939&nbsp;
looks pretty much identical to a human baby.

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:34.960
Researchers who were ordered to&nbsp;
dissect these creatures - finding out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:37.920
in the process, that they were&nbsp;
identical to human infants on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:43.520
inside, too - were offered amnestics due to the&nbsp;
understandably traumatic nature of the experience&nbsp;

00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:47.200
One of the births was stillborn, and&nbsp;
the others quickly cannibalized it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:52.640
The surviving beasts soon learned to perfectly&nbsp;
imitate the voices and behavior of human children,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:58.640
offering yet another reason that you cannot trust&nbsp;
any of your senses when it comes to SCP-939.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.640 --> 00:11:05.200
As they grew and matured, the more human parts&nbsp;
simply fell off, like a snake shedding its skin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:09.600
after a period of prolonged pain and&nbsp;
discomfort. More so than most creatures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:17.280
the Foundation contains, SCP-939’s very existence&nbsp;
is enough to cause a sense of existential dread.

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:22.160
And for a creature as full of surprises&nbsp;
as SCP-939, of course there would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:28.000
another twist in the long, red tail. You see, we&nbsp;
mentioned earlier that the SCP Foundation briefly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:35.280
considered using AMN-C227 - the amnestic gas&nbsp;
exhaled by 939 specimens - as a form of Class B&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:41.520
amnestics. However, this plan was later canceled,&nbsp;
when a horrifying side effect came to light.

00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:46.800
Amnesia is never a good feeling. Having&nbsp;
complete blank spots in your memory is actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:53.520
extremely distressing to experience. And as we&nbsp;
mentioned earlier, people exposed to AMN-C227&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:59.600
seem to experience a palpable sense of deja vu.&nbsp;
When they first experience it, it’ll be mild,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:04.640
but it’ll slowly get stronger as they&nbsp;
move towards the source. Little by little,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:10.320
you’ll feel satisfaction drawing closer,&nbsp;
until you’re wandering into a deep, dark cave.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:16.640
And before you know it, a set of red jaws are&nbsp;
closing around your neck, and it’s all over.

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:22.880
That’s right: AMN-C227 not only wipes&nbsp;
the memories of encounters with SCP-939,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:27.280
it also lures any survivors back&nbsp;
into the lair of the creatures.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.280 --> 00:12:31.120
They’ve been given the Keter Class, because&nbsp;
there’s a whole species of these things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:36.480
and even the Foundation’s best scientists can’t&nbsp;
know for sure how far their habitats extend.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:42.000
They could be waiting for you right now,&nbsp;
ready to call to you in a friendly voice.&nbsp;

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:49.280
So remember, kids, don’t believe everything&nbsp;
you hear. After all, sounds can be deceiving.

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:55.440
Now go check out “Evil Monster Created by SCP&nbsp;
Foundation SCP-2419 - The Laughing Men” and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.440 --> 00:13:02.880
“SCP-002 The Living Room &amp; the Most Terrifying&nbsp;
SCP Rooms” for more terrifying SCP creatures!

